## SQ-META31-04b | meteorite desert pyramid never placed short
@group C
@commands `[worldgen.meta_structures] log` on, new world, `/locate structure creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid` a few times, grep `meteorite_desert_pyramid` in latest.log
@pass every placed line `1/1 minecraft:desert_pyramid` plus a meteorite; short ones `not placed, core part ...` or `no satellite fitted`; none placed with `0/1 desert_pyramid`
@fails Depends on: `structures/metas #11`
@jars creativecommon
@from batches/r1101/w2_worldgen.qb
> locate structure creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid
waitlog nearest creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid is at|type "?creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid|creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid.*timed out 330
> execute positioned 6000 70 -6000 run locate structure creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid
sleep 240
> execute positioned -6000 70 6000 run locate structure creativeengineering:meta/meteorite_desert_pyramid
sleep 240
bootreject meteorite_desert_pyramid.*0/1.*desert_pyramid
look every placed line 1/1 minecraft:desert_pyramid plus a meteorite; short ones "not placed, core part" or "no satellite fitted"

## SQ-WG30-C02b | census false negatives carry a diagnosis (long: Chunky r 400 + census r 96)
@group C
@commands new world, Chunky square, `/cwglocate census 96 <x> <z>`; read `falseNegativeAt` in `kubejs/exported/worldgen/locate_census.json`
@pass every biome false negative has a diagnosis string (regenerated point, its biome, nearest-distance entries, start-piece center); record which case it shows
@fails Depends on: `structures/rates-and-groups #13`
@jars creativecommon
@from batches/r1101/w2_worldgen.qb
> tp qa 2144 200 -2592
> chunky center 2144 -2592
> chunky radius 400
> chunky shape square
> chunky start
waitlog (?i)\[Chunky\].*(task finished|finished generating|complete) 3000
> celocate census 96 2144 -2592
waitlog (?i)census.*(done|finished|written) 2400
shell python3 -c "import json,sys; d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/worldgen/locate_census.json')); s=json.dumps(d); sys.exit(0 if 'falseNegativeAt' in s else 1)"
look every biome false negative has a diagnosis string (regenerated point, biome, nearest-distance entries, start-piece centre); copy the census json into RES

